.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:2:A valid `--link` manifest record has the form `LINK  <relpath>  <target>`, but uninstall parses every record as `<sha>  <relpath>`. The resulting “relpath” contains both destination and target, so `_rel_unsafe` rejects it for containing a space. A repository installed with v1.3.0 `--link`, then upgraded to this candidate, cannot uninstall those deliveries: symlinks remain and the manifest is kept. The backup pass makes the same parsing error, so non-`.claude` link deliveries are also absent from the recovery archive. Minimal fix: parse LINK and hash records separately using the shared manifest grammar; unlink only when the current symlink target matches the recorded target, and add a v1.3 link-install → candidate-upgrade → uninstall/restore integration test.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:5:The new security refusal path reports an “incomplete” uninstall but exits 0. Automation therefore records success after a traversal record, symlinked ancestor, or every valid LINK record described above was refused. This is fail-open at the process boundary and also contradicts the documented non-success exit behavior. Minimal fix: return nonzero whenever `unsafe_count > 0`; use the documented mismatch exit for non-forced SHA mismatches, and make tests assert failure status as well as log text.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:8:The script explicitly acknowledges that the manifest is not integrity-checked, yet treats every safe-looking record as proof of framework ownership. An injected record containing the current SHA of an adopter-authored in-tree file causes that file to be deleted without `--force`. The advertised `--no-hmac-verify` option only controls backup restoration; it does not verify the install manifest. Minimal fix: have install/upgrade produce an authenticated manifest sidecar and verify it before any backup, hashing, or removal; absence or mismatch must fail closed unless the operator explicitly supplies the bypass.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:11:The pre-uninstall archive and HMAC use predictable, second-resolution paths without destination confinement or exclusive creation. A pre-existing symlink or hard link named `.claude.backup-uninstall-<timestamp>.tar.gz`—or its `.hmac` sidecar—causes the write to follow or modify another inode, potentially outside the target. Minimal fix: create unpredictable files exclusively inside a physically validated target directory, refuse linked destinations, and atomically rename only after archive and HMAC generation succeed.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:2:Concrete failure: v1.3.0’s installer never set `FMS_LINK_PATHS`, so its allow-all manifest writer could record a pre-existing adopter symlink under an enumerated directory as framework-owned. The candidate treats any unique prior `LINK` record whose live target still matches as valid provenance and emits it again. Thus a v1.3 over-claim survives upgrade/re-install; `doctor --repair` may later recreate or police an adopter-authored link.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:3:Minimal fix: do not authorize legacy `LINK` records solely by prior-record/live-target equality. Require the link to target the expected framework source for its confined relpath, or drop pre-v1.4 LINK continuity conservatively. Add a v1.3-generated polluted-manifest migration test covering both upgrade and re-install.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:10:Concrete failure: the gate claims to require a regular table, but `-f` follows symlinks. A symlinked `scripts/delivery-routes.tsv` is therefore read—and the upgrade snapshot dereferences it—without preserving evidence that its bytes came from outside the checkout. A well-formed external table can reroute an absent `.github/CODEOWNERS` to another allowed `templates/*` source and the upgrade will install those wrong bytes successfully.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:11:Minimal fix: reject a symlink leaf and symlinked components before reading or snapshotting the table, then require physical confinement to the executing checkout. Cover this with a symlink-table negative test.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:17:The ordinary copy-mode v1.3→candidate route resolves the shipped six-row table correctly; `bash -n` and `git diff --check` are clean. Release condition: before signing rc.1, close the three P1 cases and add negative fixtures proving that a polluted v1.3 LINK record is dropped and that missing, malformed, or symlinked route tables leave the target untouched with a non-zero exit.
