.claude/plans/PLAN-194/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:9:- **Conditions 1–2:** carried installer and migration debt remains material. In particular, upgrading a `user` installation can still add `availableModels`, `fallbackModel`, and `permissions.defaultMode` through ceremony-independent migration ([scripts/upgrade.sh:3729](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.r7pcp3/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3729)). This is the carried **P1, v1.4.0 condition 55**, not a new finding. Minimal fix: derive migratable settings from the selected ceremony; the declared workaround remains `--no-settings-migrate`.
.claude/plans/PLAN-194/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:16:The easiest integration detail to miss is that **adding `manual` does not make the `user` harness gate green**: its required deny entries remain absent. The release explicitly declares this limitation. Fresh installation and upgrade deliver the relocated replay fixtures; plugin packaging deliberately excludes them.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:16:   Minimal fix: pass every path as a separate `sys.argv` operand to a constant Python program; never interpolate filesystem names into `python3 -c` source.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:20:   Minimal fix: refuse when either a file or symlink already occupies `pre-push`, and document explicit chaining or installation under a distinct hook name.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:27:   Concrete scenario: the new generated derivation asserts cold-start and latency advantages—“5 ferramentas em vez de 14 cold-starts”—despite the repository’s explicit prohibition on speed or throughput claims. Generator parity merely reproduces the prohibited claim.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:36:Permitted static checks passed: Bash syntax and ShellCheck, Python AST/stdlib-only, JSON and generated-user-template parity, actionlint, diff whitespace, AGENTS freshness, count claims, and contamination. The mutating E2E harness was not rerun because this reviewer contract is read-only.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-6.txt:5:   A v1.3 adopter with an active plan has its scratchpad SQLite database under the legacy directory. After upgrade, `_state_root()` silently selects the new slug directory and opens a new empty database. `/resume` and inter-agent handoffs therefore report missing state even though the old database remains on disk. The release note only warns about the audit chain, not state stores. Minimal fix: migrate state stores during upgrade, or preserve the legacy `CEO_STATE_ROOT` until an explicit migration; document the continuity break.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-6.txt:9:   First mint is not concurrency-safe. Two sessions submitting their first prompt after upgrade can both observe no salt, generate different values, and truncate the same file at `:164`; each process then caches and uses its own value at `:215`. At least one emitted `prompt_sha256` becomes irreproducible because its salt was overwritten. Minimal fix: elect the creator with `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW`; losing processes must read and use the winner’s persisted salt.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-6.txt:13:   The new `salt-minted.json` write uses `Path.write_text`, following a pre-existing symlink and truncating its target; `chmod` at `:251` follows it again. Because v1.4 writes into an already-existing native Claude project directory, this can overwrite an adopter/tool-owned file or a file outside the state tree. Minimal fix: write a randomized `O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW` temporary file and `os.replace` it, while refusing an existing non-framework marker.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-6.txt:17:   The compatibility branch preserves legacy HMAC sidecars under `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR` and returns that directory at `:243`, but candidate writers unconditionally move their lock to the `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH` parent in `audit_emit.py:2382` and `spool_writer.py:422`. During an in-session upgrade, an old v1.3 hook locks `LOG_DIR` while a new hook locks `LOG_PATH.parent`; both append to the same log and mutate the same legacy chain sidecars. This can fork the HMAC chain or lose the chain-length increment. Minimal fix: centralize the preservation decision so key, sidecars, and lock remain under one directory, or require a quiesced atomic migration before switching locks.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-6.txt:21:   The salt event sends `project=str(runtime_paths.project_dir())`—an absolute repository path—at `:268-274`. The scrub allowlist admits `project` without value validation (`audit_emit.py:8638`), contradicting both the branch’s “slug/path never reaches the wire” claim at `audit_emit.py:6954` and the published contract at `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:501`. A first prompt can therefore record `<HOME>/private-repo` in the signed chain. Minimal fix: use a validated opaque project identifier or the existing hash prefix, and add a test asserting that no absolute path survives this action.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-6.txt:33:VERDICT: NO-GO — the scratchpad cutover, first-mint race, symlink-following write, mixed-version lock split, and false no-path audit claim must be corrected before rc.1.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-4.txt:11:Concrete failure scenario: the CHANGELOG says the seven VETO-bearing skills are undemoted, but an adopter upgrading an existing v1.3.0 installation retains the old `skillOverrides` entries. The upgrader explicitly preserves settings except enumerated additive migrations, and `skillOverrides` is not among those migrations. The upgrade reports success while veto-bearing skill bodies remain `name-only`; only a fresh installation receives the corrected profile. The four replacement `name-only` entries are likewise not consistently delivered by upgrade.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:7:- Open empty plan-state stores, reset cost accounting, and stop detecting expired credentials because legacy state is not migrated (conditions 27, 39, 40).
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:9:- Write outside the target through remaining backup, hook/schema, harness, state-store, and restore symlink/hard-link seams (43, 47, 50, 65, 69, 82).
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:31:   **FILE:LINE:** `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:499`, `:502-503`, `:530-531`; implementation at `.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:8949-8961`.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-2.txt:13:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared conditions 33, 47 and 48. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:163`, `scripts/install.sh:1453-1474`, `scripts/install.sh:2401-2410`, `scripts/install.sh:2463-2499`. Concrete failure scenario: `install_dispatcher` follows destination symlinks and unconditionally overwrites adopter-edited files; the predictable deny-baseline tempfile can redirect output outside the target; and `state/mcp_client_secrets` follows a symlinked `state/`. This also contradicts the header’s idempotence promise. Minimal fix: route all writers through the shared confinement/provenance guard and use exclusively created same-directory staging plus atomic rename.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-2.txt:17:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared condition 61. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:2046-2053`. Concrete failure scenario: any manifest line ending in two spaces plus `.github/CODEOWNERS` counts as provenance, even with an invalid digest. On a rerun, a deliberately empty CODEOWNERS may be re-rendered, silently re-enabling review routing. Minimal fix: require a regular, canonical, uniquely parsed manifest containing exactly one valid HASH record for CODEOWNERS.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-2.txt:19:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared condition 75. FILE:LINE: `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:158-195`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:251-291`. Concrete failure scenario: manifest generation walks target directories rather than an actual-delivery ledger. An untouched adopter file such as `.claude/hooks/acme_local.py` can therefore be recorded with its own hash as framework-owned and later removed by uninstall. Minimal fix: generate records solely from paths actually delivered or backed by valid ownership continuity.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-2.txt:31:- SEVERITY: P2. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:241-251`, `scripts/install.sh:936-946`, `scripts/install.sh:1114-1124`. Concrete failure scenario: the comment says the manifest helper is optional, but absence of `_framework_manifest_set.sh` now makes destination validation unavailable and refuses installation. Minimal fix: distinguish the optional hashing helper from the required confinement library.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-2.txt:43:Verification evidence: the reviewed conditions hash is `8e011bd275fe68f460ceac02df76ccd13ccc79d4a39b4d29439ec2562867e50d`; all three payload files are byte-identical to rc.1; the live table has six declared routes and six regular, non-symlink sources. Route/manifest tests passed 131/131, installer write-safety e2e passed 325/325, and the historical v1.3.0 adopter-upgrade suite passed 164/164. Bash 3.2 syntax, diff whitespace, stdlib-only, count, and version-drift checks passed.
.claude/plans/PLAN-194/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:24:Python 3.9 parsing passed for all 14 changed Python files; parser-precedence probes, Bash syntax, scoped whitespace checks and the conditions hash also passed. Review stayed offline and read-only; no full installation or live audit writes were exercised.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:11:  **Cenário:** `--settings-migrate-only` promete executar somente T5.4 e sair 0, mas os novos preflights de `docs/`, `.github/` e `SPEC/v1` executam antes do dispatch. Por exemplo, `docs` como arquivo regular causa rc 3 e impede a migração.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:28:- A condição 75, emendada neste envelope, está correta: os quatro arquivos-raiz são enumerados incondicionalmente no manifesto; um hash autoral herdado da v1.3.0 pode ser classificado `FRAMEWORK-CHANGED` e sobrescrito em [scripts/upgrade.sh:1782](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.gGzWJY/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:1782).
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-2.txt:3:The most directly applicable conditions—1, 5–14, 24, 31, 33–35, 42, 45, 47–48, 56, 60–64, 73–76, 81–82 and 84—accurately describe the candidate. Conditions 3 and 7 are link-mode residuals and do not trigger for the stated copy-mode cohort.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-2.txt:13:- **P1 — `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1263-1266`.** The new comment makes an explicit measured latency claim (“~20 ms” and “seconds”), violating `AGENTS.md:9-11`. Declared condition 24 already catches the separate “costs production nothing” claim at line 608 but not this occurrence. Minimal fix: remove the timing language and justify memoization only by avoiding repeated parsing and duplicate diagnostics.

